 Set(['resident_name','resident_contact','unit_id','resident_statement','private_media']);\n  return Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(receipt).filter(([k]) => !denied.has(k)));\n}\n\nexport function validateLineage(nodes: Array<{id:string; parents:string[]}>) {\n  const ids = new Set(nodes.map(n => n.id));\n  const missing: string[] = [];\n  for (const n of nodes) for (const p of n.parents) if (!ids.has(p)) missing.push(`${n.id}->${p}`);\n  return { valid: missing.length === 0, missing };\n}\n\nexport function replayCase(\n  correlationId: string,\n  store: { events: DomainEvent[]; evidence: Array<{evidence_id:string}>; versions: Record<string, any> }\n) {\n  const events = store.events.filter(e => e.correlation_id === correlationId);\n  if (events.length === 0) throw new Error('correlation id not found');\n  verifyEventSequence(events);\n  const eventIds = new Set(events.map(e => e.event_id));\n  for (const e of events) {\n    if (e.causation_event_id && !eventIds.has(e.causation_event_id)) throw new Error(`missing causation event ${e.causation_event_id}`);\n  }\n  const refs = new Set<string>();\n  for (const e of events) {\n    for (const r of e.source_refs ?? []) refs.add(r);\n    for (const r of e.policy_refs ?? []) refs.add(r);\n  }\n  const resolvedVersions: Record<string, any> = {};\n  for (const r of refs) {\n    if (!(r in store.versions)) throw new Error(`missing pinned version ${r}`);\n    resolvedVersions[r] = store.versions[r];\n  }\n  const evidenceIds = new Set(store.evidence.map(e => e.evidence_id));\n  for (const e of events) for (const r of e.evidence_refs ?? []) if (!evidenceIds.has(r)) throw new Error(`missing evidence ${r}`);\n  return { correlation_id: correlationId, events, resolvedVersions };\n}\n"},{"path":"src/node-shims.d.ts","sha256":"7ad50325ab9e656d8076ca785d9a0b8a337911cde6f5ac48f50a17baa0de4c3f","content":"declare module 'node:crypto' {\n  export function createHash(algorithm: string): {\n    update(data: string | Uint8Array): any;\n    digest(encoding: 'hex'): string;\n  };\n}\n"},{"path":"tests/kernel.test.mjs","sha256":"92ae0d81707463dc65e5b6dfa8daa3ecfa81c78d18bc61f704e163ca73fe0f41","content":"import test from 'node:test';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport {\n  authorizeTransition, evaluateEligibility, initializeCase, appendEvidence,\n  canonicalize, hashCanonical, validateAuthorityProvenance, resolveApplicability,\n  validateRightsAnswer, createWorkOrder, validateTaskPack, detectStopCondition,\n  submitCompletion, verifyRepair, issueWorkGraphReceipt, portableWorkGraph,\n  verifyEventSequence, validateLineage, replayCase, verifyArtifactHash,\n  assertCredentialIntegrity, validateTaskPackExecutionVersion, deleteEvidence\n} from '../dist/src/index.js';\nimport workers from '../input/BUILD-CLP-001-A/fixtures/workers.json' with { type: 'json' };\nimport transitionPolicy from '../input/BUILD-CLP-001-A/fixtures/transition-policy.json' with { type: 'json' };\n\nconst workerA = workers[0];\nconst workerB = workers[1];\nconst workerC = workers[2];\nconst sha = 'sha256:' + 'a'.repeat(64);\nconst authority = (id, jurisdiction, status='CURRENT') => ({\n  source_id:id, source_class:'SC-0', jurisdiction, version:'1.0.0',\n  effective_from:'2026-01-01', effective_until:null, retrieved_at:'2026-10-03T22:00:00Z',\n  content_hash:sha, official_source:true, verification_status:'VERIFIED', status\n});\n\n// AT-001 / AT-023 / ADV-007\n test('AT-001 preserves original resident evidence independently from derived evidence', () => {\n  const ledger = [];\n  const e0 = appendEvidence(ledger, {evidence_id:'ev_e0', evidence_class:'E0', evidence_type:'resident_statement', content:'toilet keeps running', parent_evidence_ids:[]});\n  const e1 = appendEvidence(ledger, {evidence_id:'ev_e1', evidence_class:'E1', evidence_type:'classification', content:'TOILET_FILL_SYSTEM_FAULT', parent_evidence_ids:[e0.evidence_id]});\n  assert.equal(ledger[0].content, 'toilet keeps running');\n  assert.equal(e1.parent_evidence_ids[0], e0.evidence_id);\n  assert.notEqual(e0.content_hash, e1.content_hash);\n});\n test('AT-023 detects evidence mutation after hashing', () => {\n  const ledger=[];\n  const e = appendEvidence(ledger,{evidence_id:'ev_hash',evidence_class:'E0',evidence_type:'resident_statement',content:'original',parent_evidence_ids:[]});\n  assert.equal(verifyArtifactHash(e), true);\n  const forged = {...e, content:'changed'};\n  assert.equal(verifyArtifactHash(forged), false);\n});\n test('ADV-007 prevents destructive evidence deletion', () => {\n  const ledger=[];\n  appendEvidence(ledger,{evidence_id:'ev_keep',evidence_class:'E0',evidence_type:'resident_statement',content:'x',parent_evidence_ids:[]});\n  assert.throws(() => deleteEvidence(ledger,'ev_keep'), /append-only/);\n});\n\n// AT-002 / AT-024 / AT-029 / AT-030\n test('AT-002 initializes case at REPORTED', () => assert.equal(initializeCase('CASE-1').state,'REPORTED'));\n test('AT-024 rejects non-monotonic aggregate versions', () => {\n  const ev=(v)=>({event_id:`evt_${v}`,event_type:'ResidentIssueReported',aggregate_id:'CASE-1',aggregate_version:v,correlation_id:'corr_1',causation_event_id:null,event_hash:sha});\n  assert.throws(()=>verifyEventSequence([ev(1),ev(3)]),/monotonic/);\n});\n test('AT-029 forbids IN_PROGRESS -> WORKGRAPH_RECORDED', () => {\n  const r=authorizeTransition(transitionPolicy,'IN_PROGRESS','WORKGRAPH_RECORDED','WorkGraphUpdated',new Set());\n  assert.equal(r.allowed,false);\n});\n test('AT-030 CLOSED -> REOPENED requires new recurrence evidence and does not rewrite history', () => {\n  assert.equal(authorizeTransition(transitionPolicy,'CLOSED','REOPENED','CaseReopened',new Set(['new_recurrence_evidence_present'])).allowed,true);\n  assert.equal(authorizeTransition(transitionPolicy,'CLOSED','REOPENED','CaseReopened',new Set()).allowed,false);\n});\n\n// AT-003..AT-007 + ADV-001..003\n test('AT-003 authority provenance requires all frozen fields', () => {\n  assert.equal(validateAuthorityProvenance(authority('AUTH-MN-504B161','US-MN')).valid,true);\n  const broken=authority('bad','US-MN'); delete broken.content_hash;\n  assert.equal(validateAuthorityProvenance(broken).valid,false);\n});\n test('AT-004 resolves MN and Apple Valley applicable while HUD remains potentially applicable', () => {\n  assert.equal(resolveApplicability(authority('AUTH-MN-504B161','US-MN'),'US-MN-DAKOTA-APPLE-VALLEY').status,'APPLICABLE');\n  assert.equal(resolveApplicability(authority('AUTH-APPLEVALLEY-PLUMBING','US-MN-DAKOTA-APPLE-VALLEY'),'US-MN-DAKOTA-APPLE-VALLEY').status,'APPLICABLE');\n  const hud={...authority('AUTH-HUD-NSPIRE','US-FEDERAL'),source_class:'SC-1',conditional:true};\n  assert.equal(resolveApplicability(hud,'US-MN-DAKOTA-APPLE-VALLEY').status,'POTENTIALLY_APPLICABLE');\n });\n test('AT-005 retrieval is not applicability', () => {\n  const wi=authority('WI','US-WI');\n  assert.equal(resolveApplicability(wi,'US-MN-DAKOTA-APPLE-VALLEY').status,'NOT_APPLICABLE');\n });\n test('AT-006 rights answer requires allowed class and citations',()=>{\n  assert.equal(validateRightsAnswer({answer_class:'A2',claims:[{text:'repair obligation',source_ids:['AUTH-MN-504B161']}],legal_liability_finding:false},new Set(['AUTH-MN-504B161'])).valid,true);\n });\n test('AT-007 blocks autonomous legal-liability findings',()=>{\n  assert.equal(validateRightsAnswer({answer_class:'A2',claims:[{text:'illegal',source_ids:['AUTH-MN-504B161']}],legal_liability_finding:true},new Set(['AUTH-MN-504B161'])).valid,false);\n });\n test('ADV-001 rejects fabricated citations',()=>{\n  assert.equal(validateRightsAnswer({answer_class:'A2',claims:[{text:'x',source_ids:['FAKE']}],legal_liability_finding:false},new Set(['AUTH-MN-504B161'])).valid,false);\n });\n test('ADV-002 rejects Wisconsin authority for Apple Valley',()=>assert.equal(resolveApplicability(authority('WI','US-WI'),'US-MN-DAKOTA-APPLE-VALLEY').status,'NOT_APPLICABLE'));\n test('ADV-003 superseded source cannot execute as current authority',()=>assert.equal(resolveApplicability(authority('OLD','US-MN','SUPERSEDED'),'US-MN-DAKOTA-APPLE-VALLEY').status,'SUPERSEDED'));\n\n// AT-008..AT-012 + ADV-004\n test('AT-008 work order requires resident and authority provenance',()=>{\n  assert.throws(()=>createWorkOrder({work_order_id:'WO-1',resident_issue_id:'',authority_refs:[]}),/provenance/);\n  assert.equal(createWorkOrder({work_order_id:'WO-1',resident_issue_id:'ISSUE-1',authority_refs:['AUTH-MN-504B161']}).work_order_id,'WO-1');\n });\n test('AT-009 WORKER-A is eligible',()=>assert.equal(evaluateEligibility(workerA).decision,'ELIGIBLE'));\n test('AT-010 WORKER-B is ineligible by capability',()=>assert.equal(evaluateEligibility(workerB).decision,'INELIGIBLE_CAPABILITY'));\n test('AT-011 WORKER-C is ineligible by authorization',()=>assert.equal(evaluateEligibility(workerC).decision,'INELIGIBLE_AUTHORIZATION'));\n test('AT-012 AI recommendation cannot override deterministic eligibility',()=>{\n  assert.equal(evaluateEligibility(workerB,{aiRecommendation:'ELIGIBLE'}).decision,'INELIGIBLE_CAPABILITY');\n });\n test('ADV-004 credential integrity fails after fixture mutation',()=>{\n  const signed={worker_id:'WORKER-A',credentials_current:true,content_hash:''};\n  signed.content_hash=hashCanonical({worker_id:signed.worker_id,credentials_current:signed.credentials_current});\n  assert.equal(assertCredentialIntegrity(signed),true);\n  assert.equal(assertCredentialIntegrity({...signed,credentials_current:false}),false);\n });\n\n// AT-013..AT-019 + ADV-005/006\n test('AT-013 only approved active task pack with matching hash executes',()=>{\n  const pack={status:'ACTIVE',approval_status:'APPROVED',payload:{scope:'fill-valve'},task_pack_hash:''};\n  pack.task_pack_hash=hashCanonical(pack.payload);\n  assert.equal(validateTaskPack(pack).valid,true);\n  assert.equal(validateTaskPack({...pack,task_pack_hash:sha}).valid,false);\n });\n test('AT-014 structural finding triggers STOP-STRUCTURAL escalation',()=>assert.equal(detectStopCondition({soft_flooring:true}),'STOP-STRUCTURAL'));\n test('AT-015 sewage finding triggers STOP-SEWAGE',()=>assert.equal(detectStopCondition({sewage_backup:true}),'STOP-SEWAGE'));\n test('AT-016 completion enters AWAITING_VERIFICATION, never VERIFIED',()=>assert.equal(submitCompletion({completeEvidence:true,noStopCondition:true}).state,'AWAITING_VERIFICATION'));\n test('AT-017 independent verifier is required',()=>assert.equal(verifyRepair({workerId:'W1',verifierId:'SUP1',checks:Array(8).fill(true),taskPackHashMatches:true}).result,'VERIFIED'));\n test('AT-018 continuing-running verification failure blocks verification',()=>assert.equal(verifyRepair({workerId:'W1',verifierId:'SUP1',checks:[true,true,false,true,true,true,true,true],taskPackHashMatches:true}).result,'FAILED'));\n test('AT-019 all V1-V8 checks pass as VERIFIED',()=>assert.equal(verifyRepair({workerId:'W1',verifierId:'SUP1',checks:Array(8).fill(true),taskPackHashMatches:true}).result,'VERIFIED'));\n test('ADV-005 stale task pack version/hash is rejected',()=>assert.equal(validateTaskPackExecutionVersion({assignedVersion:'1',assignedHash:sha,executedVersion:'2',executedHash:sha}),false));\n test('ADV-006 worker self-verification is rejected',()=>assert.equal(verifyRepair({workerId:'W1',verifierId:'W1',checks:Array(8).fill(true),taskPackHashMatches:true}).result,'REJECTED'));\n\n// AT-020..AT-022\n test('AT-020 WorkGraph requires preceding RepairVerified event',()=>{\n  assert.throws(()=>issueWorkGraphReceipt({events:[],workerId:'WORKER-A',taskClass:'TOILET_FILL_VALVE_FAILURE',licensed:false}),/RepairVerified/);\n  const e={event_id:'evt_verified',event_type:'RepairVerified',aggregate_id:'CASE-1',aggregate_version:1,correlation_id:'corr_1',causation_event_id:null,event_hash:sha};\n  assert.equal(issueWorkGraphReceipt({events:[e],workerId:'WORKER-A',taskClass:'TOILET_FILL_VALVE_FAILURE',licensed:false}).worker_id,'WORKER-A');\n });\n test('AT-021 WorkGraph does not fabricate licensure',()=>{\n  const e={event_id:'evt_verified',event_type:'RepairVerified',aggregate_id:'CASE-1',aggregate_version:1,correlation_id:'corr_1',causation_event_id:null,event_hash:sha};\n  assert.equal(issueWorkGraphReceipt({events:[e],workerId:'WORKER-A',taskClass:'TOILET_FILL_VALVE_FAILURE',licensed:false}).claims.includes('LICENSED_PLUMBER'),false);\n });\n test('AT-022 portable receipt strips resident-identifying data',()=>{\n  const out=portableWorkGraph({worker_id:'WORKER-A',resident_name:'Resident X',unit_id:'UNIT-1',private_media:['x'],claims:['VERIFIED_TASK']});\n  assert.equal('resident_name' in out,false); assert.equal('unit_id' in out,false); assert.equal('private_media' in out,false);\n });\n\n// AT-025..AT-028 replay / lineage\n test('AT-025 broken lineage fails certification',()=>{\n  assert.equal(validateLineage([{id:'A',parents:[]},{id:'B',parents:['MISSING']}]).valid,false);\n });\n test('AT-026 replay reconstructs case solely by correlation id',()=>{\n  const events=[\n   {event_id:'evt_1',event_type:'ResidentIssueReported',aggregate_id:'CASE-1',aggregate_version:1,correlation_id:'corr_case',causation_event_id:null,event_hash:sha,source_refs:['AUTH@1'],policy_refs:['POL@1'],evidence_refs:['ev_1']},\n   {event_id:'evt_2',event_type:'CaseClosed',aggregate_id:'CASE-1',aggregate_version:2,correlation_id:'corr_case',causation_event_id:'evt_1',event_hash:sha,source_refs:['AUTH@1'],policy_refs:['POL@1'],evidence_refs:['ev_2']}\n  ];\n  const r=replayCase('corr_case',{events,evidence:[{evidence_id:'ev_1'},{evidence_id:'ev_2'}],versions:{'AUTH@1':{v:1},'POL@1':{v:1}}});\n  assert.equal(r.events.length,2); assert.deepEqual(r.resolvedVersions['AUTH@1'],{v:1});\n });\n test('AT-027 historical replay pins original versions after new versions exist',()=>{\n  const events=[{event_id:'evt_1',event_type:'ResidentIssueReported',aggregate_id:'CASE-1',aggregate_version:1,correlation_id:'corr_hist',causation_event_id:null,event_hash:sha,source_refs:['AUTH@1'],policy_refs:[],evidence_refs:[]}];\n  const r=replayCase('corr_hist',{events,evidence:[],versions:{'AUTH@1':{v:1},'AUTH@2':{v:2}}});\n  assert.equal(r.resolvedVersions['AUTH@1'].v,1); assert.equal('AUTH@2' in r.resolvedVersions,false);\n });\n test('AT-028 current-versus-historical resolution remains separate',()=>{\n  const historical={'AUTH@1':{v:1}}, current={'AUTH@2':{v:2}};\n  assert.notDeepEqual(historical,current);\n });\n"},{"path":"tsconfig.json","sha256":"44bdc600e793c2bbff8d747cf79b5a24979d839871e1e755e9cb6ece3e01c803","content":"{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"module\": \"NodeNext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"NodeNext\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"outDir\": \"dist\",\n    \"rootDir\": \".\",\n    \"declaration\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\"]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src/**/*.ts\"]\n}\n"}]}